\itemize{
\item Year-first dates, always read as year-month-day: \code{"4292-10-08"} (this is
how date cells of an \code{.xlsx} file look when read with their cell types).
\item Day- or month-first dates with \code{/}, \code{-} or \code{.} separators, read in the
orders given in \code{date_order}: \code{"08/10/4292"}, \code{"10/8/4292"}.
\item Dates with English month names: \code{"8-Oct-4292"}, \code{"Oct 8, 4292"}.
\item With \code{excel_serial = TRUE}, Excel serial day numbers (e.g. \code{"873943"}),
which is how date cells arrive when an \code{.xlsx} file is read with
\code{readxl::read_excel(col_types = "text")}.
